<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Praia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Praia is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-verde">Cape Verde</a>, on the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> island. It grew from a sheltered harbour near the older capital of Ribeira Grande, which suffered from pirate raids, and became the colony's capital in 1770. Its old centre, the Plateau, stands on a flat-topped hill above the port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/praia.jpg" alt="Praia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xandu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pal%C3%A1cio_da_Cultura,_Praia,_Cape_Verde.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
